Constraints:
$N$ is up to $10^{12}$.
$M$ is up to $2 \times 10^4$.
$A, B$ are up to 20.
The intervals are disjoint and sorted: $R_i < L_{i+1}$.
Also $1 < L_i \le R_i < N$. This means square 1 is never bad, and square $N$ is never bad (though the condition says $R_i < N$, so $N$ is not bad).

